@startuml system-context
title logfence — System Context

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam ComponentBackgroundColor #DDEEFF
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #DDFFD0
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFEECC

actor "Application\n(any language)" as App
component "logfence-client\n(Rust library)" as Client
component "logfenced\n(daemon)" as Daemon
component "rsyslog" as Rsyslog
database "JSON Schema\nfiles" as Schemas
component "Log Storage /\nNetwork Targets" as Storage

App --> Client : calls MessageBuilder API
Client --> Daemon : RFC 5424 + JSON payload\nUnix stream socket (octet-count framed)\nor Unix datagram socket (one msg/datagram)
Daemon ..> Schemas : reads at startup\n& on SIGHUP
Daemon --> Rsyslog : validated messages\nUnix datagram or stream socket\nRFC 5424 wire format
Rsyslog --> Storage : forwards to files,\nnetwork, etc.

note right of Client
  Encodes syslog header fields
  Serializes key-value pairs to JSON
  UnixTransport: stream + octet-count framing
  UnixDatagramTransport: datagram, no framing
  Lazily connects; auto-reconnects
end note

note right of Daemon
  Validates JSON payload
  Enforces JSON Schema
  Applies CEE cookie policy
  Canonicalizes JSON (optional)
  Drops invalid messages
  Reports rejections to rsyslog
end note

note bottom of Daemon
  Invalid messages are dropped and a
  rejection report is forwarded to rsyslog
  as a warning from logfenced — they never
  reach downstream consumers.
end note

@enduml
